{% elif target.name == "index-object" %}
URI type:
  Index cache object

Default behavior:
  - `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }}` reads index cache status and capabilities.
  - Chapter-level `/index/...` URIs manage index artifacts. Archive and library `/index` URIs manage derived cache.

Use when:
  - You need to inspect, sync, or clean query cache materialization.
{% elif target.name == "job-collection-scope" %}
URI type:
  Local job collection scope

Default behavior:
  - `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }}` shows local generation jobs.
  - Use `--json` for a machine-readable job list. Job list does not support `--jsonl`; `watch --jsonl` is the streaming job interface.

Use when:
  - You need to inspect, add, or clean local generation jobs.
  - Read `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }} add --help` before enqueueing work; generation jobs can consume model/runtime cost and require `--accept-cost`.
  - Use `{{ commandName }} wikg://local/job/<job-id> watch --jsonl` for stable progress streaming.
  - Use `{{ commandName }} help runtime` for worker, log, and local state behavior.
{% elif target.name == "job-object" %}
URI type:
  Local job object

Default behavior:
  - `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }}` reads local job status.

Use when:
  - You need job status, progress, or lifecycle control.
{% elif target.name == "job-target-object" %}
URI type:
  Local job target object

Default behavior:
  - `{{ commandName }} {{ uri }}` is not a retrieval shortcut. Use `set`.

Use when:
  - You need to change an active job target.
